# rena0-air-dash-left — F1-3 fixture
# Expectations cite the recovered airborne row for Rena+0 (30) and the air-dash trigger
# the audit test uses (jump, then a double tap while airborne;
# tests/rena_animation_audit_test.cpp:197-222).
#
# The stick is RELEASED on tick 16 on purpose: row 30's travel set declares the +0x20
# hold, so holding a direction never lets the clock advance it. The body leaves that
# section on its own counter once `5 < +0x3a` and the stick is neutral
# (FUN_0043ffc0 case 0x1e :413-420), which is what drops the dash into its recovery phase
# and, with it, into the fall the port used to skip entirely (V3-30).
combo 0 0
seed 5489
spawn 0 0 0 0
spawn 1 0 0 2000
collision open-field
input 0 JUMP
input 1 -
input 12 LEFT
input 13 -
input 14 LEFT
input 16 -
expect 11 airborne 1
expect 14 dash_row 30
expect 14 anim_row 30
expect 14 air_dash_context 1
expect 14 phase 0
expect 14 y 38.5
# Recovery phase: the airborne section ends on the release rule, not on a frame timer.
expect 27 phase 2
# The recovery phase descends (0.5/tick^2, the body's +0x16); the travel phase holds y.
expect 31 y 28
# Back to the airborne state with the dash's momentum, then the ground.
expect 33 airborne 1
# The dash completes into the original's STATE 43, whose row is move 43 / set 43 — not the jump
# chain's falling row 42, whose first section is set 5 (32 frames). The port used to play set 5
# here and reach set 43 a clip later (V3-42).
expect 33 anim_set 43
expect 36 anim_set 43
# Landing enters row 44 — the shared landing row, 22 frames at the shipped 1760/4800 ticks —
# and returns to Idle's own row when the window closes (V3-42).
expect 40 anim_set 44
expect 50 anim_set 44
expect 60 anim_set 0
expect 37 state 0
expect 40 y 0
